# Product Marketing Context

**Intent:** Create and maintain `.agents/product-marketing.md` so brand, copy, and SEO rules do not re-ask basics. Not deep repositioning workshops (`brand-strategy.mdc`) or page-level copy (`marketing-copy.mdc`).

**Canonical path:** `.agents/product-marketing.md`

**Legacy paths to check:** `.claude/product-marketing.md`, `product-marketing-context.md` (in `.agents/` or `.claude/`). If found elsewhere, offer to move to `.agents/product-marketing.md`.

---

## Workflow **[core]**

### Step 1 — Check existing context

**If file exists:**
- Read and summarize what's captured.
- Ask which sections to update; only gather info for those.

**If file does not exist, offer:**

1. **Auto-draft from codebase** (recommended) — read README, landing pages, meta descriptions, about copy, `package.json`, existing docs; draft V1; user reviews and corrects.
2. **Start from scratch** — walk sections conversationally, one at a time.

Push for **verbatim customer language** — exact phrases beat polished marketing speak.

### Step 2 — Gather or draft sections

Skip sections that clearly don't apply (e.g. B2B Personas table for pure B2C).

| # | Section | Capture |
|---|---------|---------|
| 1 | Product overview | One-liner, what it does, category, type, business model |
| 2 | Target audience | Company/consumer type, decision-makers, primary use case, JTBD |
| 3 | Personas | `[applicable if B2B]` User, champion, buyer — cares / challenge / value |
| 4 | Problems & pain | Core challenge, why alternatives fail, cost, emotional tension |
| 5 | Competitive landscape | Direct, secondary, indirect competitors — how each falls short |
| 6 | Differentiation | Key differentiators, how you solve differently, why customers choose you |
| 7 | Objections & anti-persona | Top 3 objections + responses; who is NOT a fit |
| 8 | Switching dynamics | Push, pull, habit, anxiety |
| 9 | Customer language | Verbatim problem/solution phrases; words to use/avoid; glossary |
| 10 | Brand voice | Tone, style, personality adjectives |
| 11 | Proof points | Metrics, logos, testimonials, value themes |
| 12 | Goals | Business goal, conversion action, current metrics if known |

### Step 3 — Save document

Use this structure (fill all applicable sections):

```markdown
